{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 83,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A song. A Psalm of Asaph. O God, be not silent; be not speechless; be not still, O God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "See how Your enemies rage, how Your foes have reared their heads.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With cunning they scheme against Your people and conspire against those You cherish,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "saying, “Come, let us erase them as a nation; may the name of Israel be remembered no more.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For with one mind they plot together; they form an alliance against You—",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites, of Moab and the Hagrites,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "of Gebal, Ammon, and Amalek, of Philistia with the people of Tyre.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even Assyria has joined them, lending strength to the sons of Lot. Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do to them as You did to Midian, as to Sisera and Jabin at the River Kishon,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "who perished at Endor and became like dung on the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb, and all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "who said, “Let us possess for ourselves the pastures of God.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make them like tumbleweed, O my God, like chaff before the wind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As fire consumes a forest, as a flame sets the mountains ablaze,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "so pursue them with Your tempest, and terrify them with Your storm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cover their faces with shame, that they may seek Your name, O LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May they be ever ashamed and terrified; may they perish in disgrace.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.83.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May they know that You alone, whose name is the LORD, are Most High over all the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
